### Core BIOS data placement partition

| Owner | Range | Bytes | Placement contract |
| --- | --- | ---: | --- |
| Device dispatch tables and alignment | `0003h..00B0h` | 173 | bind with complete dispatch; fixed-prefix hole if moved alone |
| Saved INT 13 vectors and request scratch | `00B0h..00C3h` | 19 | retain low interface initially |
| Padding to fixed VDISK offset | `00C3h..0100h` | 61 | packing capacity, not released bytes |
| VDISK compatibility reservation | `0100h..016Ch` | 108 | fixed low address |
| AUX device index and binding | `016Ch..016Eh` | 2 | retain with GETDX contract |
| Device headers and embedded control state | `016Eh..0248h` | 218 | public real-mode pointers |
| INT 2F chain and BDS-list roots | `0248h..0250h` | 8 | public/interrupt-facing anchors |
| Disk/format request state | `0250h..026Fh` | 31 | rebind with complete disk service |
| Disk error translation tables | `026Fh..0281h` | 18 | private service data; rebind readers |
| Sector alignment | `0281h..0284h` | 3 | packing only |
| Firmware sector/bounce buffer | `0284h..0484h` | 512 | retain DMA-safe storage; not boot-only scratch |
| Four linked floppy BDS records | `0484h..0614h` | 400 | preserve public links and BPB pointers |
| Media template and character/clock state | `0614h..062Ah` | 22 | mixed constants and mutable service bindings |
| **Total** | | **1,575** | nested in the core BIOS row above |

The VDISK anchor remains at 0100h. Moving earlier tables alone leaves
a hole; savings require repacking retained owners and lowering the final
resident break. Firmware/DMA storage is not interchangeable with HMA or
extended-backed UMB merely because CPU far pointers can address it.

### Character-service placement partition

| Owner | Range | Bytes | Initial placement decision |
| --- | --- | ---: | --- |
| Console body | `082Ah..08FBh` | 209 | service candidate |
| Break interrupt and IRET | `08FBh..0902h` | 7 | retain low initially |
| Serial body | `0902h..0998h` | 150 | service candidate |
| Printer body | `0998h..0A60h` | 200 | service candidate |
| Clock state and near bindings | `0A60h..0A73h` | 19 | retain low initially |
| Clock body | `0A73h..0B6Eh` | 251 | service candidate |
| First disk state byte | `0B6Eh..0B6Fh` | 1 | outside character owner |

Service-body inventory: 810 bytes before gateways.
Shared low dispatch/exit code, CMOS helpers, ROM/A20 return gates and
device state are separate. These bodies are not position-independent;
their existing near calls and CS-relative state need explicit bindings.

### Bulk-placement design budget (not achieved savings)

| Candidate | Current bytes | Unproved prerequisite |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| BIOS_SERVICE_START..BIOS_SERVICE_END | 3,578 | split CS-relative low data, near control flow, and ROM-return gates |
| Entire DOS low prefix | 4,480 | subtract mandatory public anchors, stacks, and entry gates |
| Initial DOS-owned HMA tail | 16,892 | subtract COMMAND and every other reservation before choosing destinations |

The candidate sizes are inventories, not guaranteed gains or a sum to
subtract from VC's gap. The HMA tail is capacity, not conventional
memory; copied low allocations must be released and coalesced. Dynamic
SYSINIT allocations require the runtime census, not this linker map.
